      "message": "Actually I had considered doing just that but for a different reason. Having macros littered throughout a function greatly reduces readability, so I was thinking of using the macros to determine which function pointer to call. Something like this:\n\n#if defined(CONFIG_USB_TYPEC_VPD)\n\n    // Only call the function if sig is not SUPER\n    if (sig !\u003d SUPER)\n       ret \u003d (*tc_vpd_state_error_recovery[sig])(port);\n\n#elif defined(CONFIG_USB_TYPEC_VPD_CT)\n\n    // Or add a dummy function, for SUPER, to the table that does nothing \n    ret \u003d (*tc_vpd_ct_state_error_recovery[sig])(port);\n\n#endif\n\n     return SUPER(ret, sig, tc_state_host_open_ct_open);\n\n\nDuplicated code in the function pointers would be moved to a separate inlined function.",
